      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's common for swelling and tightness to occur in the calf after surgery, especially if the surgery involved a long incision or required significant tissue repair. The swelling you're experiencing may be due to normal post-operative inflammation. However, it's always best to consult with your doctor to rule out any potential complications or other issues, as non-weight-bearing calf swelling can be a sign of other problems. Your doctor can assess the area and provide guidance on what to do next.",
